CmdStan selection
CmdStan\set_cmdstan_path('/absolute/path/to/cmdstan-2.40.0');
echo CmdStan\cmdstan_version();
print_r(CmdStan\check_cmdstan_toolchain());
check_cmdstan_toolchain() returns the path and version of make, the C++ compiler CmdStan will use, and stanc. It throws when make or the compiler is missing. It does not install missing tools.
Without an explicit path the library first checks CMDSTAN, then chooses the highest version under ~/.cmdstan/cmdstan-*. CmdStan’s version is read from its makefile, independently of the stanc compiler version. The path must contain the CmdStan makefile and stanc executable. Run inference with absolute paths when deploying under a service account.
To install an official release:
$path = CmdStan\install_cmdstan('2.37.0', cores: 2, timeout: 1800);
The installer downloads the specified release from GitHub over HTTPS, checks archive entry paths and links, extracts in a private staging directory, builds at the final location to preserve runtime library paths, and selects the resulting installation. Without a version it installs the latest release.
CmdStan\install_cmdstan(release_file: '/downloads/cmdstan-2.40.0.tar.gz', cpp_options: ['STAN_THREADS' =&gt; true]);
CmdStan\install_cmdstan('2.40.0', overwrite: true, cores: 4);
print_r(CmdStan\cmdstan_make_local(cpp_options: ['CXXFLAGS' =&gt; '-O3']));
release_url accepts an HTTPS .tar.gz URL and release_file a local tarball. The version is then read from the archive’s top-level cmdstan-* directory. cpp_options are written to make/local before building. The installer refuses to replace an existing version unless overwrite: true; the old installation is moved aside and deleted only after the new build succeeds, and a failed build restores it. cmdstan_make_local() reads, appends to, or replaces the selected installation’s make/local. curl, tar, make, internet access, disk space, and sufficient memory are needed. Versions are explicit so an application does not unexpectedly change its statistical backend. rebuild_cmdstan(cores: 2) runs clean-all and build on the selected installation; only call it when you intend to rebuild that toolchain.

Compile a model
$model = CmdStan\cmdstan_model('model.stan', cpp_options: ['STAN_THREADS' =&gt; true]);
$model-&gt;check_syntax(stanc_options: ['warn-pedantic' =&gt; true]);
$model-&gt;compile(force_recompile: true, cores: 2);
Executables and generated headers live beside the Stan source. Use a source directory without whitespace or make metacharacters. Data and output paths can contain spaces. Source changes trigger compilation; changes in included Stan files should use force_recompile: true. Changes in the selected CmdStan installation or stanc/C++ options force a model rebuild; a fingerprint receipt beside the executable tracks those settings. Switching shared CmdStan settings may require rebuild_cmdstan().
If you already have an executable, supply exe_file and compile: false along with its Stan source. compile() requires an executable with the source’s basename.
